pref.kind.day_off
* {day} off

pref.kind.shift_pref
* {shift} shifts

pref.kind.weekend_off
* Weekend off

pref.kind.no_back_to_back
* Not two in a row

pref.kind.max_nights
* At most {n} nights

pref.kind.min_nights
* At least {n} nights

pref.kind.works_with
* Likes working with {name}

pref.kind.avoid_with
* Not with {name} this week

pref.quote.day_off
* Could I have that day off? Every week, if possible.

pref.quote.early
* Early shift, please — I'm useless after three.

pref.quote.late
* Night owl — late shift, please.

pref.quote.max_nights
* A few nights a week is plenty for me.

pref.quote.min_nights
* I need the hours.

pref.quote.weekend_off
* Weekends are for my family.

pref.quote.no_back_to_back
* Not two nights in a row, please.

pref.quote.partner
* If we could work the same nights…

staff.barista.pref.late
* Late shifts, please. I'm a different person after midnight.

staff.barista.pref.sunday
* Sunday lunch with my parents. They think I'm still at uni.

staff.barista.pref.exam
* Exam on Friday. I can't miss it.

staff.cook.pref.back
* Not two nights in a row. My back.

staff.cook.pref.full
* Full nights. Half a night is half a soup.

staff.porter.pref.cook
* Mr Holub lets me watch him bake.

staff.cashier.pref.early
* Home by half past two — my daughter wakes at night.

staff.cashier.pref.hours
* Four nights at least. I need the hours.

staff.sound_tech.pref.thursday
* Thursday's band rehearsal — and the video call home.

staff.sound_tech.pref.late
* Late, please. I sound better after midnight. So does the coffee.

staff.quiet_one.pref.tuesday
* Lectures on Tuesdays.

staff.quiet_one.pref.weekend
* Not weekends, if possible. Crowds.

staff.server.pref.bara
* With Bára, if I can. She makes the nights go fast.

staff.server.pref.max
* Five nights, no more. I've got a life to visit.

# --- coach marks (§8): Karolina's thoughts, or Lida's notes in amber italics ---------------------------------
tutorial.light_window
* The light in the window first, Karolinko. Always first.

tutorial.machine
* The old machine needs a minute to wake up. Hold it until it hums.

tutorial.greet
* That's Mirek. Grandma's oldest regular. A wave wouldn't hurt.

tutorial.take_order
* He's waiting for me. Let's see what he'd like.

tutorial.pick_recipe
* "Black, the way Lida poured it." I think I know which one.

tutorial.pour_over
* Slow circles, in time with the rain. And if it goes wrong — skip, it'll still be good.

tutorial.quick_brew
* A plain order. I can let the machine work and do something else.

tutorial.tip_coin
* Something glints on Mirek's table. He left a coin after all.

tutorial.clear_table
* Cups won't carry themselves to the sink.

tutorial.moment
* Something's glowing by the window…

tutorial.speed
* It's quiet. I could let the clock run a little faster.

tutorial.closing
* A note for tomorrow's me, then lights off at six.

tutorial.journal
* Grandma kept a box of photos behind the till. I'll keep one too. (J)

tutorial.book
* Grandma's recipes are all in here — and a card for linden tea, in her handwriting. (K)

tutorial.experiment
* Linden and honey, her card says. Into the pantry slots, then Try.

tutorial.jukebox
* Grandma's records. Three still play.

tutorial.wash
* The cups are stacking up. Hold, and they'll wash.

tutorial.mop
* Muddy footprints by the door. One good swipe.

tutorial.duties
* Kuba takes the dishes. I take the guests.

tutorial.rozpis
* He wants to work with the cook. Noted.

tutorial.rail
* A ticket with an empty ring — nobody has it. That one's mine.

tutorial.cat
* The station cat. It's been watching this door longer than I have.

tutorial.usual
* Mirek trusts me now. "The usual?" — one tap.

tutorial.atmosphere
* It feels warmer in here when the lamps are on.

tutorial.fairness
* The rings show how everyone feels about the week. Nobody needs to be stretched.

tutorial.garlands
* Windows first, then the counter, then the door. Like every year, Karolinko.
